        "title": "Study 2 — Ten trials, one direction",
        "show_image_mobile": false,
        "background_heading": "Study Background",
        "background_text": "Zoom out. Researchers pooled ten separate trials — 601 women in total — to ask whether the ovulation results hold up across all of them. They do. The authors are honest about the gap — proof for pregnancy and live-birth rates is still lacking — and so are we (Pundir et al., 2018).‡",
